<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-2870] .NET: Attribute-based SQL configuration handles nested indexed field incorrectly</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-2870</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;For nested fields (Employee.Address.Zip, for example)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;QueryEntity.fields expects dot notation: address.zip&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;QueryEntity.indexes expects only field name: zip&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;QuerySqlField(IsIndexed=true)&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; results in dot notation in both cases, which causes hang on cache creation.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
